From: Jason Rhinelander <jason@imaginary.ca>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 17:04:46 -0400
Subject: Fix includes for fmt 12 and GCC 16

fmt 12 made fmt/core.h equivalent to fmt/base.h, which doesn't declare
fmt::format, so files using it now include fmt/format.h.  GCC 16's
libstdc++ no longer pulls in <cstdlib>, <cstring> or <stdexcept>
transitively, which types.cpp relied on.
